<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">13.
<U>DAMAGE OR DESTRUCTION OF LEASED PREMISES</U>. In the event the leased premises are hereinafter partially or entirely damaged or destroyed
or rendered partially or wholly unfit for Lessee&rsquo;s use by fire, tornado, earthquake or any casualty, rent shall abate in such proportion
as the part of the premises destroyed or rendered unfit for such use bears to the total premises herein leased. If the damage or destruction
shall be so extensive as to require substantial rebuilding of the improvements on the leased premises, either party may elect to terminate
this lease by written notice to the other party. Such election must be made in writing within thirty (30) days after the occurrence of
the damage or destruction.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-left: 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

